WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.764
The workbook's seventh chapter reads
closed findings back out of ServiceNow,

2
00:00:04.764 --> 00:00:09.625
using a read-only role, and writes one of
the workbook's evidence records for each.

3
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:13.468
Approval, executing identity
and what ran are left empty,

4
00:00:13.468 --> 00:00:17.475
each with its reason, because
the first pass doesn't actuate.

5
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:19.700
Four checks run on every record.

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.888
Does the evidence still match its hash?

7
00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.250
Is there evidence at all?

8
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.038
Did the intended state match?

9
00:00:25.038 --> 00:00:26.951
And did it close inside its window?

10
00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:30.800
Five fictional records come out
with two of three closed on time.

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.799
Three have problems: one closed late, one
had its evidence edited after closing,

12
00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:38.875
and one was closed with a
note that just says done.

13
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:42.225
The workbook's design calls
that prose, not evidence.

14
00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:45.575
Each line carries the hash
of the line before it,

15
00:00:45.575 --> 00:00:48.925
so the ISSO's verifier
catches a removed record.

16
00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:52.000
The package can show tampering,
but it isn't signed.

17
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.802
A later month continues the chain
from the previous month's head,

18
00:00:55.802 --> 00:00:58.660
so the packages link from
one period to the next.
